WithFixedBudget` plus its coverage parent. The instrument therefore cannot silently add unfuzzed-in-CI targets.\\n+- FINDING (M6): a Fake leaking `time.Now` is caught by two fresh fakes disagreeing (real timestamps in the failure), not just by the sleep test — the stronger kill.\\n+- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260830-7a0s2c_secconftest.md` (6/6 AC rows with call sites, 10-row mutant table: 4 narrowing + 4 arm-deletion + 2 census-only, 10/10 killed, 0 survivors; M4 token-preserving mutant with 222-pass/1-fail full-suite run; darwin skip report skipped=0; digest `5569f34caab734eb` x3).\\n+- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (21 pkgs), `-race` exit 0, `-cover` exit 0 (secconftest 86.9%), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet` + `GOOS=windows go build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (94 cases, unchanged). 8/8 fuzz targets pass 5s smoke and `-fuzztime=100x` with no corpus written.\\n+- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/landing are orchestrator steps).\\n+\\n+### 1939 — secprim round-3 rework: C1 handle binding, C2 classify-before-close, C3 spelling bound, N24 restored\\n+- SCOPE: TASK-260830-2ciy0s round-3 (review-verdict-rev2, C1–C4 blocking). Production: `internal/secprim/nofollow.go` (`guardRootMatches` fstat dev/ino compare via `os.SameFile`, new `guard root mismatch` site in `Guard.Open`); `open_member_unix.go` (classify-before-close at both sites); spelling bound stated in `errors.go`/`inventory_test.go`/README + `TestRefusalInventorySpellingBoundIsStated`; honest reparse mapping in both windows files + README. Tests: `guard_root_test.go` (foreign-handle refusal + matched control, cross-platform), depth-3/4 full-string vectors in `open_unix_test.go`.\\n+- ROOT CAUSE (C1): `openCommitRelative(root, _ string, ...)` discarded `guard.root`; unix walked the handle, Windows the path — one entry, two containment roots. Fixed in shared `Guard.Open` so both answer identically.\\n+- ROOT CAUSE (C2): from iteration 2 `previous == current`; closing before `classifyCommitErr` fstat'd a recycled fd, misreporting depth>=2 symlink hops as `open failed`. Revert reproduces the exact reported string.\\n+- FINDING (N24): arm-drop spelling KILLS (`target special file` vs `target directory`); the `Size() > 0` spelling SURVIVES (empty dirs report Size > 0) — rev2 withdrew the wrong spelling. FINDING (D14): scripted shape is COMPILE-FAIL (unused import), superseded by killing D14b.\\n+- EVIDENCE: 5 FILE resources — `TASK-260830-2ciy0s_secprim-rev3.md` (31/31 AC rows with call sites, 22/29 rules narrowing-covered, R12 double probe, Windows escape-capable set + AF_UNIX/DEDUP counterexamples), battery py + log (59 killed/61 applied; N7 survives w/ bound), full-test + race logs.\\n+- GATES: `go test ./...` exit 0 (20 pkgs), `-cover` exit 0 (secprim 94.4%), `-race` secprim+cliresult exit 0, `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet/build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0. Tree OID `7cae2bfa` identical across battery, plants, probes, finish.\\n+- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/landing are orchestrator steps).\\n+\\n ### 1553 — Shared-environment boundary round-2 rework: admit hole closed by delegation, shape census, 27-mutant battery\\n - SCOPE: TASK-260830-3bkz0c round-2 rework (review-verdict-rev3, B1/B2/F1/F2 blocking + B2b). Freeze on sessadapter/dirnode production lifted for exactly this fix. Production: sessadapter/dirnode decodeStrictObject delegate frame verdicts to environ.DecodeStrictObject (fault translation only); buggy hasLoneSurrogateEscape/readUTF16Escape copies deleted; environ.rawUint53 hardened with trailing-data check; dead environ.validCapability deleted. Tests: frame corpus proves both directions (3 composed rows added, 7 verdicts flipped with absent-phrase pins), shape census (25 rows) + 14 synthetic controls + grammar fresh-name rule + delegation pin, environ unit tests for uint53/sorted-strings-halves/Fault rendering, both leaves' arm censuses derive the bridge from environ source.\\n - FINDING (B2): witness `\\\\\\\\ud800\\\\udc00` (escaped backslash + literal ud800 + real lone low) admitted by sessadapter.DecodeTuple (Version rewritten to `\\\\\\\\ud800`+U+FFFD) and dirnode.CheckScanRequest while environ/canonicaljson/provhost refused — the raw scan misread quoted text as a high surrogate and paired it with the following real escape. Closed by delegation, not by widening the scan. All five judges refuse post-fix (probe logs kept).\\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\\nindex 3893b0d..4c59dc6 100644\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -508,6 +508,158 @@ stdoutCap is pinned at MaxFrameBytes+2 in both directions, with a\\n maximal-frame-plus-junk probe through the production runner proving the\\n probe byte is load-bearing.\\n \\n+## Safe Process and Filesystem Primitives\\n+\\n+[`internal/secprim`](internal/secprim) implements the shared safe\\n+process and filesystem primitives of Sections 16.3, 16.4, and 16.7:\\n+no-follow path handling, staging containment, structured argv,\\n+environment allowlists, terminal control-string escaping, and secret\\n+redaction for free-text streams. It is a library behind the production\\n+launch and rendering paths, not a second authority: path grammars stay\\n+in [`internal/scalar`](internal/scalar) (the member gate delegates every\\n+shared rule there and adds only encoded dots, overlong separators, and\\n+the Windows alternate-stream, trailing-dot/space, and device rules the\\n+section names), byte-counted SpawnPlan rules stay in\\n+[`internal/provhost`](internal/provhost) (which delegates its\\n+environment-name grammar here so the two cannot drift), Structured\\n+Error detail redaction stays in [`internal/axerror`](internal/axerror),\\n+SSH argv admission stays in [`internal/config`](internal/config), and\\n+the `ax pane SESSION_ID` entrypoint rule stays in\\n+[`internal/terminalbackend`](internal/terminalbackend). Trust for\\n+external executables is deliberately not implemented here:\\n+`provider.trustCandidate` (Section 7.1, with the approving owner fact)\\n+and `terminalbackend.DigestFile` (Section 4.B trust tuple, with no owner\\n+fact) differ by contract, and a third path would be another copy, not\\n+convergence.\\n+\\n+`Guard.Resolve` maps one staging member to its lexical commit path under\\n+the member grammar plus an independent joined-prefix check (the prefix\\n+conjunct is unreachable through the entry and stays as defense in\\n+depth, pinned by a generated-corpus tripwire), an optional managed set,\\n+and Unicode case-fold collision detection. Lexical resolution alone\\n+does not contain: a symlinked intermediate directory redirects any\\n+path-string open outside the root, because `O_NOFOLLOW` constrains only\\n+the final component. The commit half is `Guard.Open`, which first binds\\n+the passed handle to the guard root (fstat device/inode compare,\\n+refusing a foreign directory handle as `guard root mismatch`\\n+identically on both platforms) and then walks every component relative\\n+to the verified `OpenNoFollowDir` root handle (`openat` with\\n+`O_NOFOLLOW` per component on unix, never re-resolving a path string;\\n+a best-effort Lstat component walk from the verified root path on\\n+Windows) and refuses a symlinked intermediate at any depth at commit\\n+time as `member symlink escape`. `OpenNoFollowFile`/`OpenNoFollowDir`\\n+open without following a trailing symlink (`O_NOFOLLOW` on unix; an\\n+Lstat gate refusing symlinks and irregular reparse points with a\\n+stated check-then-open TOCTOU bound on Windows) and re-verify shape on\\n+the descriptor; the unix open sets `O_NONBLOCK` so a FIFO refuses\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 8708,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2177,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
