{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d1fb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0779e-4d99-7252-aca0-901ba58a6e8d"},"sequence":1880,"recorded_at":1780531400003755,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"352ff598-ec69-42f2-8d2a-c94c81033676","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"352ff598-ec69-42f2-8d2a-c94c81033676","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"352ff598-ec69-42f2-8d2a-c94c81033676"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"b673fc0d-7e6c-4afa-bc63-6bfb8703ee71"},"task_id":"b673fc0d-7e6c-4afa-bc63-6bfb8703ee71","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"b673fc0d-7e6c-4afa-bc63-6bfb8703ee71","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/round1-outcome.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-7a0s2c — fixture, fuzz, and fault test infrastructure\n2|\n3|Leaf 2 of STORY-260830-1i3qu7. New package `internal/secconftest`\n4|(doc, runner, clock, crash, fuzz, hostile, skip + runner, clock,\n5|crash, fuzz, hostile, skip tests) plus 8 fuzz-validation commands in\n6|`task-board.config.json`, a README section, and a LOGBOOK entry.\n7|Leaf-1 `internal/secprim` production code is untouched.\n8|\n9|Worktree tree OID (computed, uncommitted): `9ec5199c07a6fcf6f6dfa1ee8b682ec13037b3e4`\n10|Base commit: `722ed1a8c3ac0e4169990f55318897f8e39247f0`\n11|(HEAD tree `5eb6d8a547b6efa392cdfe0c66dc2132fed96ce5`)\n12|\n13|## AC coverage: 6 of 6 rows driven through production entry points\n14|\n15|| # | AC row | Production call site | Named committed test |\n16||---|--------|----------------------|----------------------|\n17|| 1 | deterministic fixture runners | `secconftest.Runner.Run` / `Digest` | `TestRunnerDigestIsDeterministic` (digest `5569f34caab734eb` x3 runs), `TestRunnerExecutesInSortedOrder` |\n18|| 2 | fake clocks | `secconftest.Fake.Now` / `Advance` / `Set` | `TestFakeClockIgnoresRealTime` (20 ms sleep moves wall, not fake), `TestRecordingNoticesUnwiredClock` |\n19|| 3 | crash points | `secconftest.Injector.MaybeFail`, `Transactor.Prepare/Commit/Rollback` | `TestTransactorCrashOutcomes` (4 points, exact outcomes + byte state), `TestTransactorRecoversAfterFault` |\n20|| 4 | protocol fuzzing | 8 entries below | 8 `Fuzz*` targets + `TestFuzzDriversReachProduction` (22 arrivals/entry) |\n21|| 5 | hostile strings | `secprim.CheckMemberPath`, `Guard.Resolve/Open`, `DetectCaseCollision`, `CheckArgv/NewCommand`, `IsEnvName/BuildEnv`, `EscapeForTerminal`, `Redact` | `TestHostilePathMembersRefused`, `TestHostileSymlinkEscapeRefusedAtCommit`, `TestHostileArgvMembersStaySingleElements`, `TestHostileRenderMembersNeutralized`, `TestHostileRedactMembersScrubbed`, … |\n22|| 6 | platform capability skips | `secconftest.Require` / probes | `TestSkipDecideTable`, `TestSkipReportLogsHostCounts` |\n23|\n24|Negative/refusal rows (gate admits what it must reject → named test\n25|fails): unreached fixture refused (`TestRunnerRefusesUnreachedFixture`);\n26|unwired clock reads zero (`TestRecordingNoticesUnwiredClock`); wrong-section\n27|quote refused (`TestQuoteInSectionRefusals`); strict-platform absence fails\n28|(`TestSkipDecideTable`); changed-body retry → `idempotency_mismatch` with no\n29|second root (`TestTransactorIdempotentRetry`); unmanaged member refused with\n30|`ErrUnsafePath` (`TestHostileUnmanagedMembersRefused`); NUL/empty argv refused\n31|with `ErrUnsafeArgv`; rollback without prepare refused.\n32|\n33|## Fuzz targets → entry points (arrival proven by seed run)\n34|\n35|| Target | Entry | Arrivals (seed run) |\n36||--------|-------|---------------------|\n37|| FuzzCheckArgv | secprim.CheckArgv | 22 |\n38|| FuzzCheckMemberPath | secprim.CheckMemberPath | 22 |\n39|| FuzzIsEnvName | secprim.IsEnvName | 22 |\n40|| FuzzRedactCorpus | secprim.Redact | 22 |\n41|| FuzzEscapeForTerminal | secprim.EscapeForTerminal | 22 |\n42|| FuzzRenderForTerminal | secprim.RenderForTerminal | 22 |\n43|| FuzzGuardResolve | secprim.Guard.Resolve | 22 |\n44|| FuzzDetectCaseCollision | secprim.DetectCaseCollision | 22 |\n45|\n46|Arrival is established by `TestFuzzDriversReachProduction`, which drives 22\n47|seeds through the same `Driver` methods the fuzz targets call and asserts a\n48|non-zero counter per entry. 8/8 targets pass 5 s smoke and `-fuzztime=100x`\n49|with no corpus written (tree clean after). All 8 are registered in the\n50|configured validation matrix; the repo gate\n51|`TestConfiguredValidationRunsEveryFuzzTargetWithFixedBudget` failed until\n52|they were registered, so unfuzzed-in-CI targets cannot be added silently.\n53|\n54|## Mutant battery: 10 applied, 10 killed, 0 survivors\n55|\n56|| Mutant | What it narrows the gate to | Named failing test |\n57||--------|-----------------------------|--------------------|\n58|| M1 narrowing: arrival gate exempts one unreached member | zero-call class minus `\"unreached\"` | TestRunnerRefusesUnreachedFixture |\n59|| M2 narrowing: prepare-commit outcome → safe_retry | one wrong outcome admitted | TestCrashClassifyTable (+ TestTransactorCrashOutcomes) |\n60|| M3 narrowing: strict-unavailable → skip | unexpected skip passes quietly | TestSkipDecideTable |\n61|| M4 token-preserving: QuoteInSection drops section check, keeps token match | wrong-section quote admitted | TestQuoteInSectionRefusals |\n62|| M5 arm-deletion: MaybeFail never fires | no crash point exists | TestCrashPointFiresOnceWhenArmed |\n63|| M6 arm-deletion: Fake.Now returns time.Now() | wall clock leaks in | TestFakeClockStartsPinned (+ IgnoresRealTime) |\n64|| M7 arm-deletion: runner sort removed | registration order leaks in | TestRunnerExecutesInSortedOrder |\n65|| M8 arm-deletion: DriveEscape returns input | entry unreachable | TestFuzzDriversReachProduction |\n66|| M9 census: roster class renamed out of coverage | 18-class census breaks | TestHostileRosterShape |\n67|| M10 census: digest drops last fixture | execution log unwitnessed | TestRunnerDigestCoversAllFixtures |\n68|\n69|Split: narrowing 4, arm-deletion 4, census-only 2. M4 additionally ran the\n70|full behavioral suite under the mutant: 222 pass, exactly 1 fail\n71|(TestQuoteInSectionRefusals) — the kill is unconfounded and no behavior\n72|test depends on the checker. Denominator is production-derived (all mutants\n73|in `internal/secconftest` non-test files); every mutant was reverted and the\n74|package is green after each (`RESTORED-GREEN` x4 runs).\n75|\n76|Survivors: none. No bound is claimed from a survivor.\n77|\n78|## Skips on this host (darwin/arm64)\n79|\n80|`symlink ok, fifo ok, mode-bits ok, nonroot ok` — suite report\n81|`skipped=0 failed=0`. secprim + secconftest verbose run: 0 `--- SKIP`\n82|lines. An unexpected skip on a strict platform fails via `decide`.\n83|\n84|## Determinism\n85|\n86|Runner digest `5569f34caab734eb` identical across 3 processes;\n87|registration-order reversal identical; capability probes deterministic\n88|across repeat runs.\n89|\n90|## Gates (real exit codes, standalone processes)\n91|\n92|- `go test ./... -count=1` → exit 0 (21 pkgs ok)\n93|- `go test ./... -race -count=1` → exit 0\n94|- `go test ./... -cover -count=1` → exit 0 (secconftest 86.9%)\n95|- `go vet ./...` → exit 0; `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` → exit 0\n96|- `GOOS=windows go build ./...` → exit 0; `go build ./...` → exit 0\n97|- `gofmt -l internal/` → clean; `git diff --check` → clean\n98|- `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` → exit 0\n99|  (contracts=60 sections=36 cases=94 fixtures=30 compat=55;\n100|  coverage line unchanged from baseline)\n101|\n102|## Reuse (no new copies)\n103|\n104|No decoder, bound check, string measure, path handling, or escaping was\n105|written: string measure stays in `environ.StringLength`, member grammar in\n106|`scalar.ParseRelativePath`, device table in `scalar.IsReservedWindowsDeviceName`,\n107|refusals/escaping/redaction in `secprim`. Hostile members derive from the\n108|pinned spec text (`specdoc`) + Unicode tables + `scalar` predicates, never\n109|from `secprim` tables.\n110|\n111|## Stated bounds\n112|\n113|- The Transactor proves the injector/outcome/idempotency vocabulary, not any\n114|  product recovery path.\n115|- Fuzz covers Section 16 string/vector gates, not containment races or TOCTOU.\n116|- Tombstone-deletion and TOCTOU shapes have no product surface in this story\n117|  and are not driven. `path-symlink-escape` is an FS witness, not a string\n118|  corpus member (pinned by roster-shape test).\n119|- `FuzzTargetEntry` map↔target correspondence is pinned by count + arrival\n120|  tests; Go has no runtime fuzz-target registry (stated, not claimed).\n121|- No capability is advertised: the instrument cannot enable a platform lane\n122|  or provider suite.\n123|\n124|## For the next leaf (CI gates) — not board elements, prose only\n125|\n126|- The 8 `secconftest -fuzz -fuzztime=100x` commands added to\n127|  `task-board.config.json` are ready for the M0 CI leaf to execute.\n128|- Suggested follow-up (no board element created per story rule): crash-point\n129|  coverage for product journals when a product journal lands; Windows-lane\n130|  skip-count evidence from a Windows runner."}}}
